{"Title":"An Act relative to the education of the veterans of Massachusetts ","BillNumber":"H3535","DocketNumber":"HD980","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PAS1","Name":"Paul A. Schmid III","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PAS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T17:39:26.663"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PAS1","Name":"Paul A. Schmid III","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PAS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T17:39:26.6633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3535/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Schmid of Westport, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3535) of Paul A. Schmid, III for legislation to authorize free online public higher education courses to veterans.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1:  Chapter 15A of the Massachusetts General Laws, as so appearing in the 2020 official edition, are hereby amended by adding the following section:\r\n\t“Section 46:  The council shall develop and adopt a written policy requiring each public institution of higher education to offer and administer online courses free of charge to any Veteran of Massachusetts as defined by M.G.L. ch. 4, s.7, clause 43.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}